1
00:00:05,834 --> 00:00:07,501
(All characters, places, and organizations
in this drama are fictitious.)

2
00:00:07,501 --> 00:00:09,101
(Filming followed broadcast guidelines
for minors, some scenes used AI.)

3
00:00:11,027 --> 00:00:12,027
I'll go.

4
00:00:12,052 --> 00:00:13,252
(Episode 16)

5
00:00:15,912 --> 00:00:17,273
Where is your child?

6
00:00:29,154 --> 00:00:30,487
Then where is our child,

7
00:00:35,852 --> 00:00:40,495
the one you gave birth to?

8
00:00:59,854 --> 00:01:04,169
You even showed Gyu Min the ultrasound.

9
00:01:08,853 --> 00:01:11,320
You told her to wait for you
to come back with the baby.

10
00:01:15,387 --> 00:01:19,895
So where is our child?

11
00:01:34,101 --> 00:01:35,401
Somewhere up there.

12
00:01:45,647 --> 00:01:50,290
I think the little angel
lost its way for a moment.

13
00:01:52,587 --> 00:01:54,389
It came into the world and then...

14
00:01:58,201 --> 00:02:01,369
it went away again.

15
00:02:26,475 --> 00:02:28,101
Gyeol will be waiting.

16
00:02:29,461 --> 00:02:30,661
You should go.

17
00:02:41,901 --> 00:02:43,401
Please take care of him.

18
00:03:24,434 --> 00:03:27,401
Someday, when I have kids,
I'm starting a baseball team.

19
00:03:29,121 --> 00:03:31,154
Do you even know how many people
a baseball team takes?

20
00:03:31,401 --> 00:03:34,357
Of course. Nine players.

21
00:03:37,201 --> 00:03:38,794
You're going to have nine children?

22
00:03:39,184 --> 00:03:40,674
Why? Can't I?

23
00:03:40,827 --> 00:03:42,632
You can't. Absolutely not.

24
00:03:42,701 --> 00:03:45,301
Do you know how hard pregnancy
and childbirth are on a woman?

25
00:03:46,101 --> 00:03:48,601
Let's have one and raise them well.

26
00:03:50,001 --> 00:03:54,501
No way. One is too lonely.

27
00:03:57,034 --> 00:04:00,501
Five, then. A basketball team.

28
00:04:01,387 --> 00:04:04,676
Since when do you plan kids by sport...

29
00:04:05,300 --> 00:04:09,167
Badminton, then. Just two.

30
00:04:11,401 --> 00:04:15,001
That won't work. I've only picked out
one name so far.

31
00:04:15,635 --> 00:04:16,801
What is it?

32
00:04:18,701 --> 00:04:21,071
Hope. Kim Hope.

33
00:04:23,274 --> 00:04:27,338
Then the second one has to be Wish.

34
00:04:27,363 --> 00:04:29,346
Hope and Wish. How's that?

35
00:04:29,701 --> 00:04:31,001
They're beautiful.

36
00:05:10,580 --> 00:05:13,449
There. You're all dry.

37
00:05:13,520 --> 00:05:14,843
Now let's go put some lotion on you.

38
00:05:29,501 --> 00:05:34,301
That bath made you so handsome, Gyeol.

39
00:05:34,701 --> 00:05:36,101
Thank you.

40
00:05:43,034 --> 00:05:44,501
Anyone watching would think he's your son.

41
00:05:46,328 --> 00:05:48,534
Close the door. He'll get cold.

42
00:05:54,961 --> 00:05:57,594
That man is so petty.

43
00:05:58,181 --> 00:06:00,940
I told you. He's got such a small heart.

44
00:06:01,601 --> 00:06:02,955
But he's a good man at heart.

45
00:06:04,167 --> 00:06:07,667
Hey, we need to trim your fingernails
and toenails, too.

46
00:06:13,901 --> 00:06:17,933
What? Why are you staring at me again?

47
00:06:18,901 --> 00:06:21,443
Because you seem
like a really good person.

48
00:06:22,234 --> 00:06:25,105
That's why I like you a lot too.

49
00:06:26,334 --> 00:06:27,830
Are you confessing to me?

50
00:06:31,901 --> 00:06:35,946
I wish you were my dad.

51
00:06:54,774 --> 00:06:59,374
Gyu Seo was bragging about hugging you,
so I want a turn.

52
00:07:04,434 --> 00:07:08,734
You're right. It's been a while
since I hugged you, hasn't it?

53
00:07:08,759 --> 00:07:09,759
Yes.

54
00:07:13,347 --> 00:07:15,635
But why are you so skinny?

55
00:07:16,401 --> 00:07:18,425
You look even thinner than last time.

56
00:07:20,367 --> 00:07:24,467
It upsets me. You're having a hard time.

57
00:07:25,334 --> 00:07:28,001
Not at all. I weigh the same.

58
00:07:29,234 --> 00:07:31,434
It isn't that hard on me, Gyu Min.

59
00:07:32,234 --> 00:07:34,792
- No need to worry.
- Okay.

60
00:07:37,001 --> 00:07:40,669
By the way, I hear Gyeol is at Mu Jin's.

61
00:07:43,080 --> 00:07:46,150
So that's who he leans on.

62
00:07:47,161 --> 00:07:49,589
That kid really is smart.

63
00:07:50,067 --> 00:07:52,563
Smart and good at reading people.

64
00:07:53,541 --> 00:07:58,213
Mu Jin is such a great guy.
He's so kind and caring, too.

65
00:08:07,481 --> 00:08:11,144
Tell him to save you a spot
to lean on too.

66
00:08:13,434 --> 00:08:17,464
Mu Jin is desperate
to be with you right now.

67
00:08:18,234 --> 00:08:20,997
If you leave him like this,
he might really fall apart.

68
00:08:21,901 --> 00:08:23,034
Gyu Min.

69
00:08:23,280 --> 00:08:26,047
What do we do? Just leave him like this?

70
00:08:26,701 --> 00:08:28,901
We have to save a life first, don't we?

71
00:08:29,201 --> 00:08:31,958
Give him a chance. Give him some hope.

72
00:08:32,001 --> 00:08:34,301
So Mu Jin can come back to you...

73
00:08:36,401 --> 00:08:39,828
Wait. Should I just tell him?

74
00:08:40,534 --> 00:08:42,616
Kim Mu Jin is still my love...

75
00:08:43,726 --> 00:08:46,177
I mean, he's your love.

76
00:08:47,834 --> 00:08:51,680
Have you met Mu Jin?

77
00:08:53,555 --> 00:08:54,755
Yes.

78
00:08:56,175 --> 00:08:59,755
Every day. And I'll see him today, too.

79
00:09:00,934 --> 00:09:06,288
He's the owner and head chef
at the restaurant where I work.

80
00:09:10,401 --> 00:09:14,601
It's a small world,
and fate is stronger than we think.

81
00:09:15,501 --> 00:09:21,219
I think the universe made me the bridge
to bring you and Mu Jin back together.

82
00:09:22,567 --> 00:09:26,507
And here I thought I was just the crow.

83
00:09:27,901 --> 00:09:30,734
Amazing. So is Gyeol the magpie?

84
00:09:40,234 --> 00:09:41,903
Why are you eating the burned part?

85
00:09:42,934 --> 00:09:46,198
Spit it out, now.

86
00:09:49,668 --> 00:09:52,947
Are you crazy? Why would you swallow that?

87
00:09:53,434 --> 00:09:56,249
You never listen to a word I say.

88
00:09:56,301 --> 00:09:58,559
Do you know
how bad burned food is for you?

89
00:09:58,734 --> 00:10:00,501
Are you trying to die young?

90
00:10:01,801 --> 00:10:04,901
If I eat burned food twice,
you will beat me to death.

91
00:10:06,301 --> 00:10:09,676
How old are you, and you still
can't make decent scrambled eggs?

92
00:10:09,834 --> 00:10:11,591
How are you ever going to get married?

93
00:10:13,141 --> 00:10:15,976
Where do I even start with you guys? Move.

94
00:10:18,801 --> 00:10:20,003
What are you doing?

95
00:10:21,101 --> 00:10:23,201
I'll make the scrambled eggs today.

96
00:10:25,634 --> 00:10:28,106
Forget it, I've got it.
You said we'd fend for ourselves.

97
00:10:29,401 --> 00:10:32,198
You're just going to burn them again?
Eggs are expensive!

98
00:10:33,301 --> 00:10:35,653
I won't burn them.

99
00:10:37,101 --> 00:10:39,934
I'm only doing it for you today.

100
00:10:40,307 --> 00:10:42,208
I said I've got it. I can do it.

101
00:10:45,449 --> 00:10:47,101
Hey. What's going on with you two?

102
00:10:47,301 --> 00:10:51,234
Are you two throwing hands now?

103
00:10:51,334 --> 00:10:52,401
It's not like that.

104
00:10:52,634 --> 00:10:57,890
I'm at my wits' end.
What kind of children are you?

105
00:10:58,001 --> 00:11:00,326
Did I really raise you guys this badly?

106
00:11:00,801 --> 00:11:03,934
How is it that neither of you is normal?

107
00:11:05,147 --> 00:11:07,396
We weren't fighting, Dad.

108
00:11:09,134 --> 00:11:10,570
Did you check your phone?

109
00:11:11,151 --> 00:11:13,024
Gyu Yeong says she got married.

110
00:11:15,101 --> 00:11:18,067
When? When did she get married?

111
00:11:18,401 --> 00:11:19,401
No way.

112
00:11:19,501 --> 00:11:23,401
She just threw together a group chat
and posted it.

113
00:11:23,434 --> 00:11:27,456
She even attached a certificate
showing she's off my family register...

114
00:11:27,801 --> 00:11:30,601
I'm dizzy. I think I'm in shock.

115
00:11:32,234 --> 00:11:34,271
Han Gyu Yeong has completely lost it.

116
00:11:36,001 --> 00:11:38,921
I need to lie down. I'm dizzy.

117
00:11:44,734 --> 00:11:48,501
I'm married. I'm starting
to move out today,

118
00:11:48,534 --> 00:11:50,719
and I'll be moving in
with my in-laws in three days.

119
00:11:50,901 --> 00:11:53,801
Farewell dinner tonight at six
at Cheonanmun.

120
00:11:54,201 --> 00:11:56,304
If you're busy or don't want
to come, don't.

121
00:11:57,501 --> 00:12:03,042
(Certificate of Residence Registration)

122
00:12:05,801 --> 00:12:08,801
Knocking? Right. Don't bother.

123
00:12:08,901 --> 00:12:11,134
You could break the door down
and it wouldn't matter now.

124
00:12:11,901 --> 00:12:13,501
Was this really the only way?

125
00:12:14,834 --> 00:12:19,901
We lived as a family for over 30 years,
and you send one line in a chat?

126
00:12:21,701 --> 00:12:23,301
Did you really have to go this far?

127
00:12:24,901 --> 00:12:28,182
- It wasn't one line. It was several.
- Han Gyu Yeong.

128
00:12:28,334 --> 00:12:30,601
Should I hug you and sob instead?

129
00:12:30,901 --> 00:12:32,501
You wouldn't mean it.

130
00:12:32,534 --> 00:12:36,023
If I said I was leaving, you'd all
set off fireworks.

131
00:12:36,301 --> 00:12:38,534
What are you talking about?

132
00:12:38,634 --> 00:12:39,926
You said you wanted to cut ties.

133
00:12:40,126 --> 00:12:43,460
Weren't you the one who said,
forget the wedding and cut ties now?

134
00:12:44,334 --> 00:12:45,901
Why are you clinging to me?

135
00:12:47,901 --> 00:12:51,167
Do you hate this family that much?

136
00:12:51,234 --> 00:12:53,453
Why ask now? Do you like them?

137
00:12:53,601 --> 00:12:55,519
Do you love being part
of the Han family that much?

138
00:12:57,834 --> 00:13:00,834
Fine. Take care of yourself.

139
00:13:01,701 --> 00:13:04,234
I'm sorry, but I can't come
to your farewell dinner.

140
00:13:08,660 --> 00:13:12,946
And this is my last request
as your sister.

141
00:13:13,501 --> 00:13:18,934
Be honest with your husband and
his family, and ask them to forgive you.

142
00:13:19,201 --> 00:13:23,325
If they won't forgive you,
get on your knees and beg until they do.

143
00:13:24,301 --> 00:13:26,501
And if they still won't forgive you,

144
00:13:28,301 --> 00:13:30,976
the front door is always open, so...

145
00:13:31,001 --> 00:13:33,434
Is that a curse? You think I'm you?

146
00:13:34,001 --> 00:13:36,934
Forget worrying about me,
Han Gyu Rim. Look after yourself.

147
00:13:37,134 --> 00:13:40,401
You keep making your own life harder.
Raising a child who isn't even yours,

148
00:13:40,601 --> 00:13:42,701
and ruining your own future...

149
00:13:42,734 --> 00:13:44,701
Of everyone I've met in my life,

150
00:13:44,726 --> 00:13:46,660
you are the dumbest,
the most pathetic, the most clueless...

151
00:13:46,685 --> 00:13:47,718
Let's stop here.

152
00:13:47,934 --> 00:13:50,401
Any more and we'll both end up
in a hospital.

153
00:13:51,901 --> 00:13:56,801
One last request before I go,
from 32 years on the same register.

154
00:13:57,201 --> 00:13:59,401
Find Gyeol's birth parents
before he gets any older.

155
00:14:01,601 --> 00:14:06,161
And start over while you're young
and people still call you pretty.

156
00:14:06,534 --> 00:14:08,102
Look at Gyeol.

157
00:14:08,201 --> 00:14:12,201
He bolted the second he heard you weren't
his real mother. Ignoring your calls.

158
00:14:12,401 --> 00:14:13,801
After everything you've done for him, too.

159
00:14:14,301 --> 00:14:15,734
Doesn't that feel like betrayal?

160
00:14:16,034 --> 00:14:17,801
Why wait three whole days?

161
00:14:18,601 --> 00:14:21,337
Just get out right now,

162
00:14:21,901 --> 00:14:24,001
before I actually break your nose.

163
00:14:31,901 --> 00:14:35,751
I've said it over and over.
Don't take in a stray.

164
00:14:36,301 --> 00:14:39,001
Pour everything you have
into the twins and Gyeol,

165
00:14:39,001 --> 00:14:41,901
and they'll all stab you in the back.
Just watch.

166
00:14:42,301 --> 00:14:44,408
You should know who you can trust.
Why put your faith in people?

167
00:14:48,334 --> 00:14:52,701
One day the woodcutter met a tiger cub
in the mountains,

168
00:14:52,701 --> 00:14:54,534
crying with a white cloth tied
to its tail.

169
00:14:55,334 --> 00:14:59,334
"My father grieved after Grandmother
passed away,"

170
00:14:59,534 --> 00:15:04,101
"and died a few days later,"
said the tiger cub.

171
00:15:07,654 --> 00:15:10,872
- That's so sad, isn't it?
- Yes.

172
00:15:12,070 --> 00:15:16,017
The tiger really believed
he was Grandmother's son?

173
00:15:16,101 --> 00:15:19,134
Yes. But in the storybook I read as a kid,

174
00:15:19,401 --> 00:15:22,967
I think it said Grandmother
believed it was her son too.

175
00:15:23,134 --> 00:15:24,601
That's how I remember it.

176
00:15:24,801 --> 00:15:27,639
What? Grandmother thought
the tiger was her son?

177
00:15:27,740 --> 00:15:32,407
Yes. The tiger once believed he was human
because the woodcutter fooled him,

178
00:15:32,734 --> 00:15:37,901
but Grandmother thought,
"So what if he looks like a tiger?"

179
00:15:38,134 --> 00:15:39,618
"If I believe he's my son,
then he's my son."

180
00:15:39,901 --> 00:15:40,934
Seriously?

181
00:15:42,234 --> 00:15:47,701
She knew that the most important thing
isn't how you look. It's what you believe.

182
00:15:48,101 --> 00:15:49,301
"I believe in you."

183
00:15:49,534 --> 00:15:50,934
"I believe in you."

184
00:15:53,601 --> 00:15:55,034
I believe in you too, Gyeol.

185
00:15:56,301 --> 00:16:00,034
I believe you'll come to understand
how sincere your mother is.

186
00:16:03,154 --> 00:16:06,446
You're all your mother has.

187
00:16:06,761 --> 00:16:10,354
No one in the world means
as much to her as you do.

188
00:16:10,801 --> 00:16:14,781
So jealous. Seriously jealous.

189
00:16:18,534 --> 00:16:23,245
I can't skip work again today, so I'm
asking Gyu Seo to look after you.

190
00:16:23,507 --> 00:16:24,837
Any objections? Raise your hand.

191
00:16:25,830 --> 00:16:27,143
No objections?

192
00:16:29,201 --> 00:16:32,134
Look at him. Mention a watch,
and he finally picks up.

193
00:16:33,401 --> 00:16:36,865
I'm in the hospital lobby.
I'll be right up.

194
00:16:39,534 --> 00:16:43,734
I've never seen such a piece of shit.

195
00:17:00,701 --> 00:17:02,313
Hey, you've gained weight.

196
00:17:04,101 --> 00:17:05,601
It's just swelling.

197
00:17:06,234 --> 00:17:09,455
Hey, you already got the teeth done.

198
00:17:11,101 --> 00:17:13,000
They're temporary.

199
00:17:14,255 --> 00:17:16,676
Either way, I'm sorry about what happened.

200
00:17:16,701 --> 00:17:18,801
Violence is never okay,
no matter the circumstances.

201
00:17:22,234 --> 00:17:27,001
I don't want to talk to you right now,
so just give me the watch and go.

202
00:17:31,734 --> 00:17:37,001
Here. The Patek Philippe limited edition
you wanted so badly.

203
00:17:37,534 --> 00:17:39,042
I sent the certificate by message.

204
00:17:39,201 --> 00:17:42,966
Only three of these came
into the country, right?

205
00:17:43,087 --> 00:17:45,610
That's right. You watch freak.

206
00:17:47,601 --> 00:17:49,601
Beautiful.

207
00:17:51,001 --> 00:17:56,701
If I catch you cheating one more time...

208
00:17:56,801 --> 00:17:59,256
you might end up with a full set
of dentures. Got it?

209
00:18:02,534 --> 00:18:05,301
Did you come to threaten me or apologize?

210
00:18:05,701 --> 00:18:09,401
Who are you anyway?
Why are you butting into my family?

211
00:18:09,401 --> 00:18:11,443
Gyu Yeong and I aren't strangers.

212
00:18:12,769 --> 00:18:14,000
What does that mean?

213
00:18:16,401 --> 00:18:19,001
Are you two having an affair
behind my back?

214
00:18:19,001 --> 00:18:21,021
You think I'm like you, asshole?

215
00:18:21,508 --> 00:18:23,516
Then what are you saying?

216
00:18:25,701 --> 00:18:30,701
Why do I go overboard
whenever it's about Gyu Yeong?

217
00:18:30,901 --> 00:18:33,201
I thought that was strange,
so I looked into it.

218
00:18:34,001 --> 00:18:37,301
Turns out Gyu Yeong is...

219
00:18:37,501 --> 00:18:42,901
my father's great-aunt's
niece's uncle's aunt's daughter.

220
00:18:43,067 --> 00:18:45,613
Blood really does run thick.

221
00:18:46,601 --> 00:18:49,801
What are you talking about?

222
00:18:49,834 --> 00:18:51,901
Anyway, Gyu Yeong and I aren't strangers.

223
00:18:53,134 --> 00:18:55,901
What? Why is this guy here?

224
00:18:56,001 --> 00:18:57,134
Hey, you're here.

225
00:18:59,501 --> 00:19:01,732
Why do you let just anyone into the room?

226
00:19:01,757 --> 00:19:02,973
Don't you have any shame?

227
00:19:03,301 --> 00:19:04,847
He didn't just let me in.

228
00:19:05,001 --> 00:19:08,601
He let me in because I offered him
a watch. That cheap bastard.

229
00:19:08,734 --> 00:19:09,734
Heung Sik.

230
00:19:10,501 --> 00:19:12,501
Are you actually related to him?

231
00:19:13,521 --> 00:19:17,676
Me? Am I crazy? Related, my foot.

232
00:19:17,701 --> 00:19:18,901
We're related, Gyu Yeong.

233
00:19:19,034 --> 00:19:21,934
We're blood relatives.
I'm your distant cousin.

234
00:19:22,001 --> 00:19:23,734
So call me big brother from now on.

235
00:19:24,101 --> 00:19:27,201
Sorry, but I've never
had a brother like you.

236
00:19:27,401 --> 00:19:31,087
And Seong Uk needs complete rest,
so could you please leave?

237
00:19:32,401 --> 00:19:36,720
Fine. I came to apologize,
so I'll apologize and go.

238
00:19:43,001 --> 00:19:49,441
Something like this
could happen again someday,

239
00:19:49,466 --> 00:19:54,701
so straighten up,
you good-for-nothing bastard.

240
00:19:59,282 --> 00:20:00,534
I'll go.

241
00:20:10,301 --> 00:20:11,743
Cho Heung Sik!

242
00:20:19,234 --> 00:20:20,234
Follow me.

243
00:20:22,201 --> 00:20:23,521
No.

244
00:20:24,387 --> 00:20:25,720
That damn man, honestly.

245
00:20:28,801 --> 00:20:33,576
If you don't listen to me,
I'll torment Han Gyu Rim, 115 times worse.

246
00:20:33,601 --> 00:20:36,134
Thumbtacks in her shoes,
cockroaches in her pillow.

247
00:20:36,801 --> 00:20:38,899
So you'd better come with me.

248
00:20:41,301 --> 00:20:43,503
What is that? A grade-schooler?

249
00:20:46,101 --> 00:20:48,454
I'm tired.

250
00:20:57,881 --> 00:20:59,781
Your eyes will split. Stop glaring.

251
00:21:00,094 --> 00:21:03,976
You're crazy about Han Gyu Rim.
Like her that much? Then propose.

252
00:21:04,074 --> 00:21:09,274
Gyu Rim and I are just friends.
Friendship.

253
00:21:09,301 --> 00:21:11,934
Enough. I don't care about you two.

254
00:21:12,034 --> 00:21:14,309
Why do you keep butting
into other people's business?

255
00:21:14,334 --> 00:21:17,776
And that cousin business earlier?
Why are you my brother?

256
00:21:17,801 --> 00:21:19,601
We really are related, Gyu Yeong.

257
00:21:19,834 --> 00:21:24,155
We're descendants of the same ancestor.
Children of Dangun.

258
00:21:24,601 --> 00:21:28,314
I barely got off the family register.
Now I have to renounce my nationality?

259
00:21:28,807 --> 00:21:31,907
I think you keep fussing over me
because I'm Han Gyu Rim's sister,

260
00:21:32,134 --> 00:21:35,068
but I've registered my marriage
and left that family register.

261
00:21:35,234 --> 00:21:37,674
And as of eight this morning,
Han Gyu Rim and I...

262
00:21:37,701 --> 00:21:40,701
have completely cut ties.
We're total strangers now.

263
00:21:41,301 --> 00:21:43,083
- Is that right?
- That's right!

264
00:21:47,201 --> 00:21:49,409
She isn't the enemy
who killed your parents,

265
00:21:49,434 --> 00:21:52,334
so for family who share the same blood
to cut ties like this...

266
00:21:52,534 --> 00:21:53,876
Does that make any sense?

267
00:21:53,901 --> 00:21:57,323
Why do you keep butting into my business?
And don't give me any advice.

268
00:21:57,580 --> 00:22:00,209
I hear the settlement cost you
an arm and a leg,

269
00:22:00,234 --> 00:22:02,901
so if you've got time to meddle,
go make some money.

270
00:22:03,101 --> 00:22:07,425
Show your face in front of me again
and I'll let snakes loose in your house.

271
00:22:12,234 --> 00:22:16,813
Fine. I'll stay out of it.
You're not my sister anyway.

272
00:22:19,901 --> 00:22:23,181
If you were my sister, I'd have broken
your legs. That girl.

273
00:22:29,734 --> 00:22:30,901
Mine.

274
00:22:34,812 --> 00:22:36,101
Are you unhappy that I came?

275
00:22:39,001 --> 00:22:40,534
You don't want me here?

276
00:22:40,734 --> 00:22:42,399
You don't miss anyone in the family?

277
00:22:42,934 --> 00:22:46,201
I missed you and Gyu Min too.

278
00:22:47,534 --> 00:22:49,342
Thank you so much, Gyeol.

279
00:22:52,001 --> 00:22:55,067
Want some apple pie?
Mu Jin made it before he left.

280
00:22:55,280 --> 00:22:56,897
Whatever you want.

281
00:23:00,034 --> 00:23:01,913
Why does blood type matter so much?

282
00:23:02,780 --> 00:23:03,780
What?

283
00:23:04,501 --> 00:23:05,872
Just talking to myself.

284
00:23:08,801 --> 00:23:10,431
I don't think it matters at all.

285
00:23:11,401 --> 00:23:14,588
Unless you need a blood transfusion,
why does it matter so much?

286
00:23:15,091 --> 00:23:16,494
Were you talking to me?

287
00:23:17,401 --> 00:23:18,982
No, just talking to myself.

288
00:23:23,501 --> 00:23:25,001
I miss my mom.

289
00:23:27,778 --> 00:23:29,001
So go see her.

290
00:23:30,667 --> 00:23:33,830
I miss her, but I don't want to.

291
00:23:36,903 --> 00:23:38,401
It isn't like there's no way at all.

292
00:23:39,601 --> 00:23:40,946
You could see her in secret.

293
00:23:41,292 --> 00:23:42,965
You just can't get caught.

294
00:24:06,991 --> 00:24:09,316
That spy lady is back again.

295
00:24:09,471 --> 00:24:12,248
I told you loud and clear...

296
00:24:12,250 --> 00:24:14,684
not to come anywhere near here.
How dare you come back?

297
00:24:15,604 --> 00:24:18,198
Where do you think you're going?
Running away, you spy?

298
00:24:20,055 --> 00:24:21,770
Why are you back again?

299
00:24:21,830 --> 00:24:23,207
Just to drive me crazy?

300
00:24:23,254 --> 00:24:26,162
Like last time, you complained
that the kimchi was too salty,

301
00:24:26,187 --> 00:24:28,374
too bland, too sweet, too sour.

302
00:24:30,804 --> 00:24:33,293
- I have something to ask you.
- Ask what?

303
00:24:34,495 --> 00:24:36,823
Where's the police station around here?

304
00:24:37,314 --> 00:24:41,236
Got orders to plant a bomb
and need to know what to do?

305
00:24:42,725 --> 00:24:45,562
You have an employee named Han Gyu Rim,
right?

306
00:24:46,025 --> 00:24:49,256
Could you just tell me where she lives?

307
00:24:50,297 --> 00:24:52,124
I'd forgotten about that.

308
00:24:52,791 --> 00:24:55,911
You asked about Han Gyu Rim last time too.

309
00:24:56,124 --> 00:24:57,720
When I asked her,

310
00:24:57,888 --> 00:24:59,904
she said she didn't know anyone like you.

311
00:25:00,198 --> 00:25:02,024
Said you weren't related or anything.

312
00:25:04,947 --> 00:25:06,170
Who are you?

313
00:25:08,711 --> 00:25:11,656
You really aren't from North Korea?

314
00:25:12,890 --> 00:25:15,990
Ma'am.

315
00:25:16,084 --> 00:25:17,638
Ma'am!

316
00:25:19,131 --> 00:25:21,317
Ma'am, your hard days are over.

317
00:25:21,691 --> 00:25:25,577
You've met your lucky star
and your life is completely set now.

318
00:25:27,197 --> 00:25:29,444
What nonsense is this at this hour?

319
00:25:29,764 --> 00:25:31,230
And what is this lottery ticket?

320
00:25:31,264 --> 00:25:34,477
Yesterday I had an incredible dream.

321
00:25:34,643 --> 00:25:39,582
Two golden pigs were swimming
through a blue sea,

322
00:25:39,666 --> 00:25:41,729
and then they dove under.

323
00:25:42,431 --> 00:25:46,960
And suddenly they turned into dragons
and rose to the sky!

324
00:25:47,901 --> 00:25:50,585
- The pigs turned into dragons?
- Yes.

325
00:25:50,610 --> 00:25:53,415
How could I have that dream
and not buy a lottery ticket?

326
00:25:53,417 --> 00:25:55,977
So here they are. Two golden pigs.

327
00:25:55,979 --> 00:25:59,810
I bought two. One for you, one for me.

328
00:26:00,117 --> 00:26:03,392
<i>You've Won</i>

329
00:26:03,394 --> 00:26:05,931
<i>- A Gift For You</i>
- Listen,

330
00:26:06,177 --> 00:26:07,557
so,

331
00:26:08,676 --> 00:26:12,904
what are you after this time,
showing up with lottery tickets?

332
00:26:13,455 --> 00:26:17,097
I heard you're our landlord.

333
00:26:18,071 --> 00:26:21,325
Do you know that if you throw out
a lucky tenant like me,

334
00:26:21,711 --> 00:26:24,904
you'll be throwing out your luck, too.

335
00:26:25,511 --> 00:26:28,417
My fortune says I'm the swallow
that brings back the magic seed.

336
00:26:28,544 --> 00:26:29,987
Enough.

337
00:26:30,309 --> 00:26:34,117
You should have
raised your children better.

338
00:26:34,537 --> 00:26:36,056
Look at my Heung Sik.

339
00:26:36,731 --> 00:26:38,547
Raised without a father,

340
00:26:38,861 --> 00:26:42,384
he still grew up perfect in every way.

341
00:26:43,050 --> 00:26:45,003
But your daughters,

342
00:26:45,050 --> 00:26:47,726
how can they make it so obvious...

343
00:26:47,728 --> 00:26:51,444
that they grew up without a mother?

344
00:26:51,484 --> 00:26:52,484
You're right.

345
00:26:53,254 --> 00:26:55,656
They're grown and do whatever they want,

346
00:26:56,724 --> 00:26:58,324
and treat me like dirt.

347
00:26:59,657 --> 00:27:01,657
You know I'm the outcast in my family?

348
00:27:02,704 --> 00:27:04,384
They aren't children. They're enemies.

349
00:27:05,743 --> 00:27:08,616
No need to whine about it.

350
00:27:09,043 --> 00:27:11,491
You give birth to a child,
not to their heart.

351
00:27:14,763 --> 00:27:18,290
This one was asking me for your address.

352
00:27:21,164 --> 00:27:23,437
This man is Han Gyu Rim's father,

353
00:27:23,558 --> 00:27:26,097
so ask him.

354
00:27:27,912 --> 00:27:31,465
As for the house,
let's check this ticket first,

355
00:27:31,660 --> 00:27:33,452
and talk about it after.

356
00:27:37,784 --> 00:27:41,690
Why does that woman keep talking down
to me when we're both aging?

357
00:27:42,150 --> 00:27:44,588
What, is she throwing her weight
around because she's the landlord?

358
00:27:46,876 --> 00:27:48,817
I hear you asked for my address.

359
00:27:49,246 --> 00:27:50,315
Who are you?

360
00:27:54,830 --> 00:27:57,407
Who are you,
and why were you looking for me?

361
00:27:59,406 --> 00:28:00,742
Could it be,

362
00:28:02,843 --> 00:28:04,696
Mrs. Cha?

363
00:28:06,860 --> 00:28:09,144
If not, it must be Mrs. Oh!

364
00:28:12,131 --> 00:28:14,343
You still haven't broken that habit?

365
00:28:18,336 --> 00:28:20,391
Are you going to keep living
like this until you die?

366
00:28:23,284 --> 00:28:25,400
How long has it been
since we've seen each other,

367
00:28:26,094 --> 00:28:27,657
and you can't say one kind thing?

368
00:28:29,197 --> 00:28:30,862
I thought you'd come back to me,

369
00:28:31,507 --> 00:28:33,140
and I was so excited.

370
00:28:33,810 --> 00:28:35,542
I'd sooner die with my face in a dish...

371
00:28:35,996 --> 00:28:38,804
than ever go back to you.

372
00:28:39,457 --> 00:28:40,782
I've tried that,

373
00:28:41,663 --> 00:28:44,309
but it's hard to drown yourself in a dish.

374
00:28:44,777 --> 00:28:46,390
It's easier just to come back.

375
00:28:48,617 --> 00:28:50,510
I'll keep it short.

376
00:28:51,352 --> 00:28:55,757
I heard the landlord wants you
to move out?

377
00:28:58,803 --> 00:29:00,121
It's fine.

378
00:29:00,314 --> 00:29:04,594
That woman sounds harsh,
but she's soft underneath.

379
00:29:05,797 --> 00:29:09,521
I'll go whine at her a few more times
and it'll be fine.

380
00:29:11,237 --> 00:29:13,230
Don't whine at her.

381
00:29:13,482 --> 00:29:14,804
I'll get you a house.

382
00:29:16,151 --> 00:29:17,151
What?

383
00:29:18,408 --> 00:29:19,629
You'll get me a house?

384
00:29:19,764 --> 00:29:21,531
Outside Seoul, not in it.

385
00:29:22,004 --> 00:29:23,557
As far from Seoul as possible.

386
00:29:24,424 --> 00:29:26,937
I'll get you a field to farm
and make a living.

387
00:29:27,017 --> 00:29:29,617
And a boat if you'd rather be a fisherman.

388
00:29:29,642 --> 00:29:32,917
No. I'm staying in Seoul, no matter what.

389
00:29:33,604 --> 00:29:36,182
These days, once you leave Seoul,
you can't come back.

390
00:29:36,184 --> 00:29:38,417
When are you going to grow up?

391
00:29:38,973 --> 00:29:42,250
You don't even have a place to live,
and you're still being picky?

392
00:29:42,796 --> 00:29:44,583
If I tell you to leave, just leave,

393
00:29:44,624 --> 00:29:45,957
and take all the kids with you.

394
00:29:50,326 --> 00:29:53,961
Hey, am I someone who stays
when you say stay,

395
00:29:54,203 --> 00:29:55,976
and leaves when you say leave?

396
00:29:56,684 --> 00:29:59,163
Did you come to lord your money over me?

397
00:30:01,751 --> 00:30:04,130
You're about to hurt a pride
I didn't even have.

398
00:30:09,826 --> 00:30:11,143
Please leave.

399
00:30:12,770 --> 00:30:14,045
I'm begging you.

400
00:30:14,831 --> 00:30:17,184
I'm begging you like this.

401
00:30:17,363 --> 00:30:19,367
Please, Han Seok Jung.

402
00:30:20,428 --> 00:30:22,436
Please leave.

403
00:30:26,417 --> 00:30:28,150
Then give me a reason to leave.

404
00:30:30,210 --> 00:30:31,210
Why?

405
00:30:31,917 --> 00:30:35,343
Is it hard on you if I'm in Seoul?

406
00:30:37,803 --> 00:30:40,540
Are you tempted to come back to me?

407
00:30:43,098 --> 00:30:44,344
You didn't know?

408
00:30:45,377 --> 00:30:47,259
Love always comes back around.

409
00:30:50,304 --> 00:30:53,588
It's not because of you.
It's because of Gyu Rim.

410
00:30:54,577 --> 00:30:57,965
I'm afraid she'll keep suffering
if she stays in Seoul.

411
00:30:58,358 --> 00:31:01,924
I can't bear to see her keep suffering.

412
00:31:02,744 --> 00:31:04,784
What are you talking about?

413
00:31:08,121 --> 00:31:12,677
There's someone Gyu Rim shouldn't
be seeing.

414
00:31:14,037 --> 00:31:16,788
Out of sight, out of mind.

415
00:31:18,130 --> 00:31:21,381
Please, let's stop hurting Gyu Rim.

416
00:31:22,427 --> 00:31:26,490
Let's not let her get hurt. Please.

417
00:31:26,690 --> 00:31:29,957
Han Seok Jung, I'm begging you.

418
00:31:32,077 --> 00:31:35,405
Please, I'm begging you.

419
00:31:39,582 --> 00:31:43,156
The braised potatoes, the perilla stew,

420
00:31:43,181 --> 00:31:46,412
the kimchi pancake,
and the whole radish kimchi,

421
00:31:47,012 --> 00:31:48,810
that comes to fifty-one dollars.

422
00:31:48,812 --> 00:31:50,771
- I'll just make it fifty.
- My son...

423
00:31:53,224 --> 00:31:54,755
Thank you. The payment went through,

424
00:31:54,757 --> 00:31:57,014
and we'll call you again when we deliver.

425
00:31:57,651 --> 00:31:59,298
- Yes, thank you.
- Sure.

426
00:32:00,279 --> 00:32:01,790
Thank you, sir.

427
00:32:02,754 --> 00:32:05,676
How much is that one?

428
00:32:07,544 --> 00:32:10,394
- Should I show you the catalog?
- No, just that one.

429
00:32:10,909 --> 00:32:12,913
I want to buy it for my big sister.

430
00:32:13,437 --> 00:32:15,177
How many months can I split
the payments over?

431
00:32:17,558 --> 00:32:18,910
Let's go, Gyu Seo.

432
00:32:19,118 --> 00:32:21,278
Already? Did you see enough of your mom?

433
00:32:21,324 --> 00:32:22,986
What if she catches us?

434
00:32:23,150 --> 00:32:27,184
I should go. The more I look at her,
the more I want to see her.

435
00:32:30,770 --> 00:32:34,339
Don't tell my mom I was here.

436
00:32:36,086 --> 00:32:37,304
It's a secret.

437
00:32:54,942 --> 00:32:56,770
- Hello.
- Hello.

438
00:32:58,010 --> 00:33:00,569
- Good luck today.
- Take care.

439
00:33:08,791 --> 00:33:13,376
Gyeol, I miss you so much.

440
00:33:23,077 --> 00:33:26,705
(Kim Mu Jin)

441
00:33:47,016 --> 00:33:49,732
I hope today is a little easier on you.

442
00:34:04,565 --> 00:34:05,802
Thank you.

443
00:34:12,816 --> 00:34:14,894
- Pick one.
- Pick what?

444
00:34:16,700 --> 00:34:19,210
Whatever will get you talking.

445
00:34:19,344 --> 00:34:21,852
So much is happening to you right now,

446
00:34:21,854 --> 00:34:25,297
and I, your roommate and best friend,
don't know a single thing.

447
00:34:28,341 --> 00:34:32,942
You used to tell me everything,
big or small,

448
00:34:32,944 --> 00:34:35,524
and talk your worries through with me,

449
00:34:35,549 --> 00:34:39,810
but somewhere along the way, you zipped
your lips shut and stopped updating me.

450
00:34:41,951 --> 00:34:44,315
You know how much I love meddling.

451
00:34:44,340 --> 00:34:46,961
And you're not just anyone.

452
00:34:46,996 --> 00:34:49,944
You're the friend I swore
I'd marry our kids off someday.

453
00:34:53,970 --> 00:34:56,823
If the head chef and the owner
both get drunk,

454
00:34:56,867 --> 00:34:58,023
who runs dinner service?

455
00:34:58,250 --> 00:35:02,489
We've made our employees so independent,
they do better without us. Don't worry.

456
00:35:03,084 --> 00:35:05,169
Fine. What do you want to know?

457
00:35:06,088 --> 00:35:08,804
Everything. All of it.

458
00:35:08,928 --> 00:35:11,090
How long is Gyeol staying at our place,

459
00:35:11,144 --> 00:35:12,697
what you're doing about Seo Hyeon,

460
00:35:12,699 --> 00:35:14,471
what you plan to do about Gyu Rim,

461
00:35:14,471 --> 00:35:16,790
and when Kim Mu Jin turns
into Jang Mu Jin.

462
00:35:17,688 --> 00:35:20,126
It's exhausting to say.
Should I write it on a board?

463
00:35:20,151 --> 00:35:22,551
You're good at writing answers when
someone sets the problem, problem child.

464
00:35:26,047 --> 00:35:29,311
All right. You should know.

465
00:35:33,951 --> 00:35:37,653
So Gyu Rim...

466
00:35:42,351 --> 00:35:43,937
Seo Hyeon's mother...

467
00:35:50,744 --> 00:35:52,122
And then what?

468
00:35:52,310 --> 00:35:55,264
Gyu Rim, what? Seo Hyeon's mother, what?

469
00:35:55,304 --> 00:35:58,097
Don't tell me Gyu Rim is
Seo Hyeon's mother's real daughter.

470
00:36:02,442 --> 00:36:04,789
What? Seriously?

471
00:36:06,078 --> 00:36:07,941
Did I get it right again?

472
00:36:08,198 --> 00:36:12,424
(Chairman Jang Hun Tae)

473
00:36:14,088 --> 00:36:15,615
(Hong Ok Seon)

474
00:36:18,617 --> 00:36:21,037
- What now?
- Let's get hangover soup.

475
00:36:21,316 --> 00:36:23,815
I sent you the address. Come now.

476
00:36:24,051 --> 00:36:25,531
Forget it. I'm not up for it.

477
00:36:25,844 --> 00:36:29,004
If you don't come,
I'll tell Seo Hyeon all about your lies.

478
00:36:29,291 --> 00:36:31,017
Hey, come on...

479
00:36:31,444 --> 00:36:33,910
Don't bring your driver. Take a taxi.

480
00:36:34,071 --> 00:36:35,437
What? Hello...

481
00:36:39,884 --> 00:36:43,061
- Here you are. Enjoy.
- Thank you.

482
00:36:43,086 --> 00:36:46,627
The broth here is unreal.

483
00:36:46,652 --> 00:36:50,236
It'll pull every drop
of last night's alcohol out of you.

484
00:36:50,564 --> 00:36:52,962
This is great over rice,

485
00:36:52,964 --> 00:36:55,614
but wrapped in radish strips,
it's to die for.

486
00:36:55,909 --> 00:36:57,114
Eat.

487
00:36:58,086 --> 00:36:59,410
Now tell me.

488
00:37:00,144 --> 00:37:02,415
What is this? Even dressed like that,

489
00:37:02,924 --> 00:37:06,010
did your company go under overnight?

490
00:37:06,657 --> 00:37:08,334
It's fun.

491
00:37:08,901 --> 00:37:10,772
Coming somewhere nobody knows me,

492
00:37:10,797 --> 00:37:14,479
having a good bowl of spicy noodles
and heading home.

493
00:37:15,030 --> 00:37:17,111
Once you get hooked, it's hard to quit.

494
00:37:17,946 --> 00:37:18,946
Eat.

495
00:37:21,149 --> 00:37:22,743
It's getting soggy. Eat up.

496
00:37:26,424 --> 00:37:28,522
You get stranger with age.

497
00:37:33,950 --> 00:37:34,964
This is good.

498
00:37:34,966 --> 00:37:36,594
- Good, isn't it?
- Yes.

499
00:37:36,629 --> 00:37:38,061
Right.

500
00:37:38,301 --> 00:37:40,012
I should bring Yun Hui next time.

501
00:37:40,037 --> 00:37:41,531
She loves noodles.

502
00:37:43,677 --> 00:37:46,470
Isn't it more fun for you two this way?

503
00:37:46,830 --> 00:37:50,304
Sneaking around like a secret romance
behind Seo Hyeon's back.

504
00:37:57,079 --> 00:38:00,524
So why did your wife get divorced?

505
00:38:01,373 --> 00:38:04,497
You were widowed, but she wasn't.

506
00:38:05,997 --> 00:38:07,250
I never asked.

507
00:38:08,204 --> 00:38:09,900
- You never asked?
- No.

508
00:38:11,504 --> 00:38:13,724
Hello.
You're with someone different today.

509
00:38:13,725 --> 00:38:14,985
Yes.

510
00:38:15,688 --> 00:38:19,309
The man who's been coming with you
is waiting in line outside.

511
00:38:22,590 --> 00:38:24,600
I mentioned you were here,

512
00:38:24,602 --> 00:38:28,079
and he asked if he could join you.

513
00:38:28,218 --> 00:38:31,205
I'm with a friend today.

514
00:38:31,982 --> 00:38:33,750
- All right.
- Yes.

515
00:38:35,043 --> 00:38:36,850
- Never mind. Eat.
- Who is it?

516
00:38:38,896 --> 00:38:40,508
So strange.

517
00:38:48,206 --> 00:38:51,102
I'm sorry, but she's with another guest,

518
00:38:51,127 --> 00:38:53,010
so I'm afraid you can't join her.

519
00:38:54,610 --> 00:38:57,577
- Did you say it was me?
- Of course.

520
00:38:58,450 --> 00:39:02,283
Did you tell her I'm so worn out...

521
00:39:03,245 --> 00:39:04,786
I can't stand up, and I'm exhausted,
and it's hot,

522
00:39:05,407 --> 00:39:08,083
and I'm irritated and in pain?

523
00:39:08,314 --> 00:39:10,057
Well, that part...

524
00:39:11,049 --> 00:39:12,434
What?

525
00:39:18,037 --> 00:39:20,384
(Danimgil Noodles)

526
00:39:20,409 --> 00:39:22,864
You have to eat it with rice like this.

527
00:39:22,865 --> 00:39:24,671
There are too many noodles.

528
00:39:24,790 --> 00:39:27,413
Try the rice like this. It's amazing.

529
00:39:27,834 --> 00:39:29,270
All right.

530
00:39:32,833 --> 00:39:34,073
This tastes different too.

531
00:39:34,098 --> 00:39:35,281
- Good, isn't it?
- Yes, it's good.

532
00:39:35,306 --> 00:39:37,235
- Try more rice instead of noodles.
- Sure.

533
00:39:38,545 --> 00:39:39,957
Grouper lady,

534
00:39:41,151 --> 00:39:43,150
I really think I'm about to pass out,

535
00:39:43,224 --> 00:39:45,197
so could you let me join your table?

536
00:39:45,690 --> 00:39:47,655
I'll sit quietly in this corner,

537
00:39:47,756 --> 00:39:49,882
eat one bowl of noodles and go,

538
00:39:50,674 --> 00:39:53,984
so if you'll allow it just once,
I'll never forget the kindness.

539
00:39:55,694 --> 00:39:58,090
All right. Sit down.

540
00:39:59,558 --> 00:40:00,945
- Thank you.
- Sure.

541
00:40:01,073 --> 00:40:02,218
Thank you.

542
00:40:09,751 --> 00:40:11,982
I haven't eaten a thing all day,

543
00:40:13,286 --> 00:40:15,310
and I've had a rough day.

544
00:40:17,371 --> 00:40:19,391
The sun was blazing, and it was hot,

545
00:40:20,909 --> 00:40:26,002
and if I'd stood for one more second,
I would've collapsed.

546
00:40:29,470 --> 00:40:32,798
Have some cold water first.

547
00:40:36,343 --> 00:40:38,945
Did something bad happen?

548
00:40:41,149 --> 00:40:43,039
Please don't ask me anything today.

549
00:40:45,891 --> 00:40:50,125
I'm going to pour my sorrow and my rage,

550
00:40:51,546 --> 00:40:56,242
and my regrets into this bowl
and swallow it all.

551
00:40:57,588 --> 00:40:58,937
- Excuse me,
- Yes.

552
00:40:58,939 --> 00:41:02,949
- One more spicy noodle soup, please.
- Yes.

553
00:41:03,802 --> 00:41:05,004
Extra large.

554
00:41:05,157 --> 00:41:08,485
- Yes, extra large, please.
- Extra large.

555
00:41:20,998 --> 00:41:22,416
Are you crying?

556
00:41:26,219 --> 00:41:27,477
Thank you.

557
00:41:31,021 --> 00:41:33,537
Should I order you a Coke?

558
00:41:34,557 --> 00:41:36,453
No, I don't drink Coke.

559
00:41:37,917 --> 00:41:40,518
- Could we get a lemon-lime soda?
- Yes.

560
00:41:44,517 --> 00:41:46,229
What happened?

561
00:41:46,391 --> 00:41:48,004
What on earth happened?

562
00:41:49,746 --> 00:41:51,484
The years I've lived,

563
00:41:53,276 --> 00:41:55,217
I regret them all so much.

564
00:41:57,373 --> 00:41:59,617
You regret things often.

565
00:42:00,264 --> 00:42:03,620
You even miss those days
when you ate tuna all the time.

566
00:42:05,083 --> 00:42:06,317
Just once,

567
00:42:07,142 --> 00:42:10,684
if I could turn back time just once,
how good would that be?

568
00:42:12,141 --> 00:42:15,564
Then I'd really pull myself together.

569
00:42:18,631 --> 00:42:22,490
I wouldn't have let my ex-wife
go like that.

570
00:42:23,503 --> 00:42:26,522
- Your lemon-lime soda.
- Thank you.

571
00:42:33,163 --> 00:42:35,371
I feel sick. I can't eat any more.

572
00:42:37,957 --> 00:42:39,612
Thank you for letting me sit.

573
00:42:40,424 --> 00:42:43,070
- Sorry to impose on you like this.
- Not at all.

574
00:42:43,095 --> 00:42:46,863
If your stomach is off,
have some soda before you go.

575
00:42:47,457 --> 00:42:48,690
Have some.

576
00:42:48,803 --> 00:42:52,536
I don't drink Coke or lemon-lime soda,

577
00:42:53,271 --> 00:42:54,851
only sparkling water.

578
00:43:01,355 --> 00:43:02,597
Thank you.

579
00:43:07,857 --> 00:43:10,215
- How much?
- Ten dollars.

580
00:43:16,075 --> 00:43:17,369
Thank you.

581
00:43:23,324 --> 00:43:24,589
What was that?

582
00:43:25,648 --> 00:43:30,910
Hey, is that the man who said
you look ten years younger?

583
00:43:37,438 --> 00:43:39,161
Anyway, in a lot of ways,

584
00:43:39,495 --> 00:43:42,104
he doesn't seem normal, so be careful.

585
00:43:43,031 --> 00:43:44,864
He's more normal than you.

586
00:43:44,951 --> 00:43:47,744
Why does he call you "Grouper Lady?"

587
00:43:54,971 --> 00:43:56,497
Chairwoman Hong, I'm sorry.

588
00:43:56,870 --> 00:43:58,777
- I have to get going.
- Why?

589
00:43:59,777 --> 00:44:02,757
Never mind. Could you call me a taxi?

590
00:44:02,758 --> 00:44:04,208
- Hey!
- I have to make a call.

591
00:44:04,210 --> 00:44:05,404
Finish eating.

592
00:44:05,405 --> 00:44:12,405
(Danimgil Noodles)

593
00:44:15,610 --> 00:44:17,713
I'm going to tell Seo Hyeon everything.

594
00:44:18,764 --> 00:44:20,370
What Seo Hyeon and I have matters,

595
00:44:21,189 --> 00:44:25,184
but what you two have matters more.

596
00:44:27,116 --> 00:44:29,132
You can't. All right?

597
00:44:29,163 --> 00:44:32,858
I can't stand that Seo Hyeon...

598
00:44:33,280 --> 00:44:36,311
- doesn't love or respect you anymore.
- Please pick up, honey.

599
00:44:41,084 --> 00:44:42,790
(Husband)

600
00:44:59,254 --> 00:45:00,497
Mom.

601
00:45:18,197 --> 00:45:20,124
I hope I didn't pull you away from work.

602
00:45:20,883 --> 00:45:23,314
Nothing matters more to me
than you right now.

603
00:45:23,646 --> 00:45:25,050
Should we eat out tonight?

604
00:45:25,357 --> 00:45:27,777
A great Pyongyang cold noodle place
opened near my office.

605
00:45:31,237 --> 00:45:33,826
When will my mom feel better?

606
00:45:34,167 --> 00:45:35,320
Should I dance for you?

607
00:45:35,878 --> 00:45:39,537
Right, Mom. Your favorite Lee Moon Sae
announced a concert.

608
00:45:40,590 --> 00:45:41,590
Seo Hyeon.

609
00:45:43,461 --> 00:45:49,206
I've never met a man as fine,

610
00:45:50,213 --> 00:45:52,464
and good as your father.

611
00:45:55,051 --> 00:45:57,090
Did Jang Hun Tae gaslight you?

612
00:45:58,823 --> 00:46:00,624
Snap out of it, Mom.

613
00:46:01,211 --> 00:46:02,891
Dad is a very bad man.

614
00:46:02,916 --> 00:46:04,804
Lying to his wife, lying to his child,

615
00:46:04,924 --> 00:46:08,844
shameless, irresponsible, despicable,
and a total hypocrite.

616
00:46:08,891 --> 00:46:11,564
Your father lied because of me.

617
00:46:12,157 --> 00:46:13,987
To protect me,

618
00:46:14,564 --> 00:46:16,496
he took all of it on himself.

619
00:46:18,497 --> 00:46:19,815
What are you talking about?

620
00:46:22,580 --> 00:46:26,204
Mu Jin isn't your father's son.

621
00:46:27,431 --> 00:46:29,364
How could that make any sense?

622
00:46:31,724 --> 00:46:32,724
Mom...

623
00:46:33,732 --> 00:46:38,918
Mu Jin is the son of your father's friend,
Chairwoman Hong Ok Seon.

624
00:46:39,749 --> 00:46:41,656
Nothing more, nothing less.

625
00:46:44,977 --> 00:46:47,679
Why would he tell a lie like that?

626
00:46:48,770 --> 00:46:50,714
Why would Dad protect you?

627
00:46:53,004 --> 00:46:55,107
What did you do?

628
00:47:09,657 --> 00:47:11,490
The girl Mu Jin was seeing...

629
00:47:12,817 --> 00:47:14,925
Honey.

630
00:47:16,004 --> 00:47:18,249
Honey, wait. Yun Hui, wait a moment.

631
00:47:18,504 --> 00:47:19,504
Han Gyu Rim.

632
00:47:19,739 --> 00:47:22,924
Let's talk with me.

633
00:47:23,057 --> 00:47:25,444
- Seo Hyeon, go inside.
- What about Han Gyu Rim?

634
00:47:26,091 --> 00:47:28,515
Honey, don't.

635
00:47:28,624 --> 00:47:30,599
Han Gyu Rim is my daughter.

636
00:47:32,411 --> 00:47:33,617
What?

637
00:47:36,157 --> 00:47:41,164
Gyu Rim is the daughter
I left behind when I divorced.

638
00:47:49,717 --> 00:47:53,317
What are you saying right now?

639
00:47:54,001 --> 00:47:55,776
Is it true? Dad?

640
00:48:12,678 --> 00:48:14,678
It's true.

641
00:48:17,603 --> 00:48:19,043
Dad.

642
00:48:19,543 --> 00:48:23,324
Seo Hyeon, don't get worked up.
I'll explain everything.

643
00:48:23,349 --> 00:48:25,597
- Seo Hyeon.
- Get out!

644
00:48:25,864 --> 00:48:28,350
Seo Hyeon. Jang Seo Hyeon.

645
00:48:28,691 --> 00:48:32,323
Get out of my sight right now, Ko Yun Hui.

646
00:48:50,491 --> 00:48:54,792
I haven't had a drop,
so why do I feel completely wasted?

647
00:48:59,385 --> 00:49:00,613
Let me go over it again.

648
00:49:00,638 --> 00:49:04,636
So first,
the Chairman isn't your birth father,

649
00:49:04,737 --> 00:49:10,016
and Seo Hyeon's mother left Gyu Rim
behind when she divorced,

650
00:49:10,263 --> 00:49:14,837
which is why she fought you
and Seo Hyeon to the death.

651
00:49:16,790 --> 00:49:19,624
Right, that makes more sense.

652
00:49:19,823 --> 00:49:23,548
Much more sense than the Chairman
being your birth father.

653
00:49:24,364 --> 00:49:27,086
I'll check the kitchen and head home.

654
00:49:30,443 --> 00:49:33,810
So you've been going back and forth
between sisters?

655
00:49:35,297 --> 00:49:37,523
No blood between them,
but they're still sisters.

656
00:49:41,117 --> 00:49:43,772
Then Gyeol shouldn't stay at our place.

657
00:49:44,002 --> 00:49:47,456
Keep him at our place
and you two will end up tangled again.

658
00:49:49,884 --> 00:49:53,895
That kid becomes the thread, the regret,
the glue that brings you two back...

659
00:49:53,920 --> 00:49:56,054
Shut your mouth.

660
00:49:56,188 --> 00:49:58,615
Stop making predictions.

661
00:50:07,243 --> 00:50:10,350
Gyeol, you're with Gyu Seo right now?

662
00:50:12,211 --> 00:50:16,810
Tell him I'm heading in now,
so he can go home.

663
00:50:18,277 --> 00:50:20,084
All right, see you soon.

664
00:50:30,044 --> 00:50:31,580
Yes, Gyu Seo.

665
00:50:33,501 --> 00:50:36,715
You? At Mu Jin's place?

666
00:50:37,037 --> 00:50:41,500
Yes, Mu Jin asked me to be with Gyeol,
and now I'm on my way out,

667
00:50:42,280 --> 00:50:44,895
but earlier Gyeol and I went by your shop.

668
00:50:45,157 --> 00:50:47,623
Gyeol came all the way to the shop?

669
00:50:47,710 --> 00:50:51,163
Yes. He said he missed you.

670
00:50:51,652 --> 00:50:53,349
We hid and watched.

671
00:50:54,570 --> 00:50:56,876
How about you come pick Gyeol up now?

672
00:50:57,230 --> 00:50:59,963
I don't think he'll avoid you anymore.

673
00:51:00,384 --> 00:51:02,799
And I feel like we're putting
Mu Jin out too much.

674
00:51:03,898 --> 00:51:07,250
All right. I'll come.

675
00:51:42,383 --> 00:51:43,776
Leaving already?

676
00:51:47,084 --> 00:51:49,189
Did you come home early because of Gyeol?

677
00:51:49,837 --> 00:51:53,519
No, we didn't have many customers today.

678
00:51:57,258 --> 00:51:58,543
What brings you here?

679
00:51:59,784 --> 00:52:01,204
Nothing's wrong, is it?

680
00:52:03,110 --> 00:52:04,821
I came to pick up Gyeol.

681
00:52:05,957 --> 00:52:07,933
I owe you so much.

682
00:52:10,750 --> 00:52:12,521
Have you talked to Gyeol?

683
00:52:13,871 --> 00:52:17,775
No, I'm going to try now.

684
00:52:19,191 --> 00:52:22,244
All right. Don't be nervous,

685
00:52:22,771 --> 00:52:24,404
and don't be too afraid.

686
00:52:26,350 --> 00:52:28,829
You've raised Gyeol so well...

687
00:52:29,149 --> 00:52:33,137
He's much more mature and understanding
than Jeong Woo, especially for his age.

688
00:52:36,009 --> 00:52:37,239
Go up and talk to him.

689
00:52:37,264 --> 00:52:38,904
I'll wait on the first floor.

690
00:52:43,003 --> 00:52:44,578
Thank you, Mu Jin.

691
00:53:14,717 --> 00:53:17,874
Sending the door code
in case Gyeol is asleep.

692
00:53:18,536 --> 00:53:22,664
And his room is the one you see
straight ahead from the living room.

693
00:54:20,464 --> 00:54:22,091
Mu Jin, you're back?

694
00:54:34,624 --> 00:54:35,950
Gyeol,

695
00:54:37,903 --> 00:54:39,296
it's Mom.

696
00:54:43,423 --> 00:54:48,936
I came because I have something
to tell you.

697
00:54:53,196 --> 00:54:54,916
There was a time...

698
00:54:57,337 --> 00:55:00,003
when I was having a very hard time.

699
00:55:03,383 --> 00:55:09,555
It was as dark as if every light
in the world had gone out,

700
00:55:10,854 --> 00:55:13,680
and I was in so much pain...

701
00:55:15,810 --> 00:55:18,544
I couldn't take a single step.

702
00:55:27,870 --> 00:55:31,064
And that was when you came to me.

703
00:55:33,058 --> 00:55:38,391
You were crying,

704
00:55:40,623 --> 00:55:42,932
and I was a first-time mother,

705
00:55:47,143 --> 00:55:50,470
so I didn't know how to comfort you.

706
00:55:51,490 --> 00:55:54,083
So I just held you.

707
00:55:55,397 --> 00:55:57,739
And do you know what happened?

708
00:55:58,790 --> 00:56:01,457
You stopped crying,

709
00:56:02,092 --> 00:56:04,201
and there in my arms,

710
00:56:05,381 --> 00:56:07,889
you fell fast asleep.

711
00:56:09,377 --> 00:56:12,136
Looking at you sleeping,

712
00:56:13,884 --> 00:56:17,506
it felt like the whole world lit up again.

713
00:56:24,151 --> 00:56:27,411
I thought this baby had come to save me.

714
00:56:28,703 --> 00:56:33,768
Do you know how grateful I was to you?

715
00:56:34,589 --> 00:56:36,536
For this baby,

716
00:56:38,117 --> 00:56:40,784
I swore I'd do everything I could to live.

717
00:56:42,745 --> 00:56:44,658
That's what I thought.

718
00:56:46,476 --> 00:56:50,360
I lived because of you, Gyeol,

719
00:56:51,949 --> 00:56:53,480
and I still do.

720
00:56:56,922 --> 00:56:58,529
I'm so sorry...

721
00:57:00,090 --> 00:57:02,576
I couldn't give birth to you,

722
00:57:07,642 --> 00:57:09,750
I'm sorry, Gyeol.

723
00:57:12,703 --> 00:57:14,390
I'm so sorry.

724
00:57:23,804 --> 00:57:29,056
Did I really come to save you?

725
00:57:32,304 --> 00:57:36,769
Do you really live because of me?

726
00:57:41,857 --> 00:57:44,946
Yes, that's how it felt.

727
00:57:45,564 --> 00:57:48,214
Thank you for believing me, Gyeol.

728
00:57:51,535 --> 00:57:55,695
I'm going to be the tiger
who repays a kindness.

729
00:58:01,930 --> 00:58:05,019
Thank you for raising me, Mom.

730
00:58:31,784 --> 00:58:35,191
- Gyu Rim.
- I'll pack Gyeol's things and come down.

731
00:58:35,484 --> 00:58:37,284
Thank you, Mu Jin.

732
00:58:38,483 --> 00:58:39,650
Sure.

733
00:58:48,177 --> 00:58:51,900
Your reservation was an hour ago.

734
00:58:51,960 --> 00:58:53,962
Are they on their way?

735
00:58:55,210 --> 00:58:57,723
No, they aren't coming.

736
00:58:58,643 --> 00:59:01,346
- One bowl of black bean noodles.
- Sorry?

737
00:59:01,903 --> 00:59:06,449
You booked a room for eight
for one bowl of noodles?

738
00:59:08,877 --> 00:59:11,724
The most expensive dishes here,
numbers one through six,

739
00:59:11,749 --> 00:59:13,848
from here to here.

740
00:59:13,873 --> 00:59:16,737
And a bottle of Chinese liquor.
The priciest one you've got.

741
00:59:16,836 --> 00:59:18,150
Happy now?

742
00:59:18,865 --> 00:59:20,772
Yes, understood.

743
00:59:28,845 --> 00:59:32,732
Fine, Dad could be sulking and not come,

744
00:59:32,951 --> 00:59:34,788
the twins could skip it too.

745
00:59:35,148 --> 00:59:37,212
Han Gyu Rim said from the start
she wasn't coming.

746
00:59:38,929 --> 00:59:40,754
But Han Gyu O, that...

747
00:59:44,727 --> 00:59:46,094
(Han Gyu O)

748
00:59:51,077 --> 00:59:54,197
The recipient has restricted
incoming calls.

749
00:59:55,959 --> 00:59:59,349
Han Gyu O, did you just block me?

750
00:59:59,526 --> 01:00:02,702
I'm getting married and want
one last meal together,

751
01:00:02,962 --> 01:00:04,668
and you have the nerve to blow me off?

752
01:00:05,339 --> 01:00:07,439
After everything I did for you,

753
01:00:07,464 --> 01:00:11,395
back when I was in middle school
and you were in grade school,

754
01:00:11,469 --> 01:00:14,235
I gave you Honey Butter Chips,
unopened, when they were hard to get.

755
01:00:16,649 --> 01:00:18,716
Where's the bell?

756
01:00:19,151 --> 01:00:21,430
Bring me something to drink first.

757
01:00:38,704 --> 01:00:39,931
Why did you come?

758
01:00:41,192 --> 01:00:42,592
You told me to.

759
01:00:43,559 --> 01:00:46,244
- And if I told you to go, you'd go?
- Yes.

760
01:00:46,863 --> 01:00:48,669
What kind of person are you?

761
01:00:48,879 --> 01:00:51,235
You come when told, go when told,

762
01:00:51,367 --> 01:00:55,574
date when told, sleep with me when told.

763
01:00:56,166 --> 01:00:58,526
Where did you take Kwon Hui Na?

764
01:00:58,614 --> 01:01:00,267
Why didn't you answer my calls?

765
01:01:00,504 --> 01:01:02,796
I didn't think answering all that...

766
01:01:02,821 --> 01:01:05,421
was part of what you paid me for.

767
01:01:05,556 --> 01:01:07,372
Do you hear yourself?

768
01:01:08,357 --> 01:01:10,183
Then why did you call Kwon Hui Na?

769
01:01:10,760 --> 01:01:12,223
Did you think I wouldn't lose it?

770
01:01:13,125 --> 01:01:14,498
How are you so shameless?

771
01:01:14,525 --> 01:01:16,897
What makes you so great,
with nothing to your name?

772
01:01:17,680 --> 01:01:19,166
You're the one who broke the rules,

773
01:01:19,735 --> 01:01:21,528
and if you don't like it, say so now.

774
01:01:21,694 --> 01:01:23,247
I'll give back every cent you paid me.

775
01:01:34,846 --> 01:01:38,691
If it isn't you, anyone will do.

776
01:01:40,442 --> 01:01:41,563
Happy?

777
01:01:48,527 --> 01:01:51,094
(That gigolo)

778
01:01:58,243 --> 01:02:00,197
(Kwon Hui Na)

779
01:02:03,614 --> 01:02:07,780
Why did you leave me
and run away eight years ago?

780
01:02:10,481 --> 01:02:12,160
I never ran away.

781
01:02:12,982 --> 01:02:14,386
You're the one who ran.

782
01:02:16,416 --> 01:02:17,496
Is that Hui Na?

783
01:02:19,793 --> 01:02:20,793
Hey.

784
01:02:21,956 --> 01:02:25,420
Kwon Hui Na, I bought Han Gyu O
with my money.

785
01:02:25,867 --> 01:02:29,587
If you don't like us together,
pay that money back yourself.

786
01:02:49,921 --> 01:02:52,108
A leopard doesn't change its spots.

787
01:02:53,214 --> 01:02:55,540
Han Gyu O, you filthy bird.

788
01:02:56,011 --> 01:03:00,580
Wait and see. I'll snap your wings
and your legs clean off.

789
01:03:04,284 --> 01:03:06,979
- Su Chan.
- Why are you calling?

790
01:03:07,826 --> 01:03:10,133
I didn't think you'd pick up. Thank you.

791
01:03:10,239 --> 01:03:12,566
Hang up! I'm never picking up again.

792
01:03:14,392 --> 01:03:16,116
You really want to hit me, don't you?

793
01:03:16,647 --> 01:03:17,967
Then hit me. Right now.

794
01:03:18,226 --> 01:03:21,569
I won't say a word. I'll take it
until you're done.

795
01:03:36,775 --> 01:03:40,604
This isn't the way to our house.

796
01:03:44,957 --> 01:03:46,877
Where are we going?

797
01:03:47,703 --> 01:03:48,703
Gyeol.

798
01:03:51,210 --> 01:03:57,148
Should the three of us go somewhere
nobody knows us and live together?

799
01:04:39,304 --> 01:04:41,698
(Love on the Menu)

800
01:04:41,723 --> 01:04:44,136
Gyu Rim, are you seeing Mu Jin again?

801
01:04:44,161 --> 01:04:45,193
You two agreed to date again?

802
01:04:45,218 --> 01:04:48,731
I'm so happy. This is so much fun.

803
01:04:48,756 --> 01:04:50,797
If I just disappear, everything is solved.

804
01:04:50,822 --> 01:04:52,748
Mu Jin and Jeong Woo both knew,

805
01:04:52,773 --> 01:04:54,617
and made a fool of me this whole time?

806
01:04:54,642 --> 01:04:56,002
Just try meeting Seo Min Ju.

807
01:04:56,110 --> 01:04:57,729
Then you die and I die.

808
01:04:57,754 --> 01:04:58,758
Do you like me?

809
01:04:58,783 --> 01:05:01,075
How could Gyu O do this?

810
01:05:01,100 --> 01:05:02,586
If Gyu Rim finds out...

811
01:05:02,626 --> 01:05:03,919
Gyu Rim will lose her mind.

812
01:05:03,944 --> 01:05:06,137
Don't let anything shake you.

813
01:05:06,273 --> 01:05:09,126
Look only at me and listen only to me.

814
01:05:11,769 --> 01:05:13,569
Dramaday.me
